quran[29]{c,v,t}:
  81,1,"When the sun is rolled up (and darkened),"
  81,2,"when the stars scatter (and fall from their galaxies),"
  81,3,"when the mountains are blown away (after turning to dust),"
  81,4,"when the pregnant camels are left unattended,"
  81,5,"when the wild beasts are assembled together,"
  81,6,"when the seas are set on fire,"
  81,7,"when the souls are paired (again with their bodies),"
  81,8,"when the female infant, buried alive, is asked,"
  81,9,for what sin was she slain?
  81,10,"When the records (of deeds) are unfolded,"
  81,11,"when the heavens are stripped away,"
  81,12,"when the Hellfire is set ablaze,"
  81,13,"and when Paradise is brought closer,"
  81,14,then each soul will know what (deeds) it has brought along (with it).
  81,15,"So I swear by those (stars and planets) which recede (after appearing),"
  81,16,"those which move freely (in their orbit) and (then) hide,"
  81,17,"and (I swear) by the night, as it withdraws (gradually),"
  81,18,"and by the dawn, as it breathes,"
  81,19,"this (Qur’an) is indeed the word of (God, delivered by Gabriel,) a noble messenger,"
  81,20,"full of strength, (and) held in honour by the Lord of the Throne."
  81,21,"(He is) well obeyed (in the heavens), and trustworthy as well."
  81,22,"And, (O people,) your guide (Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him) is not insane."
  81,23,He surely saw him upon the clear horizon.
  81,24,And he (i.e. the Esteemed Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) is not ungenerous in disclosing (the knowledge of) the Unseen.
  81,25,And this (Qur’an) is not the word of a cursed Satan.
  81,26,So where are you going?
  81,27,"Indeed, this (Qur’an) is just a Reminder for all nations,"
  81,28,(especially) for the one among you who wishes to be steadfast (on the right path).
  81,29,"But you cannot wish (to do so) unless Allah, the Lord of all worlds, pleases."
